            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter retrieval of intracoronary detached angioplasty guidewire segment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A transcatheter technique of removing a detached angioplasty guidewire segment from the diagonal branch of the left anterior descending coronary artery is described. A standard 0.014 angioplasty guidewire was modified into a &quot;snare&quot; apparatus for retrieval of the detached wire segment. The retrieval was successfully accomplished without intimal dissection, plaque hemorrhage, or vessel occlusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
